---
/* FilterBar: the one filter for every list in Keia Atlas (rule P1, docs/rules/platform.md).
   A find box, then pill buttons (Region, Office, Kind...) that open a list of choices on hover, on click or
   tap, and on keyboard focus. Pick as many as you like. Each choice shows how many items it would leave.
   The list changes as you pick, and the address bar follows (?region=emea,apac&q=x) so a filtered list can
   be shared. It never fetches anything, never moves the page (window.rsHold) and moves items with the
   shared motion tokens (window.rsMotion); with reduced motion on, nothing moves.

   How a page uses it:
     1. Mark each thing to filter with data-fi (a card, a row, a list item). Give it:
          data-find="words to match"          every word typed must appear (any case)
          data-f-<key>="value"                one per facet; several values with a bar: "a|b"
          data-t-<key>="1"                    for a switch (toggles) when the item is on
        Keep keys in lower case with hyphens. Items inside a [hidden] panel are not counted, so the same
        items can appear as cards and as rows and only the view on show is counted.
     2. Optionally mark a container data-fb-group. It hides when none of its items show.
     3. Render the bar first in .content, above the items:
          <FilterBar placeholder="Find a space, number or office" noun={['space', 'spaces']} scope=".content"
            facets={[{ key: 'region', label: 'Region', options: [{ value: 'emea', label: 'EMEA', sub: 'optional' }] }]}
            views={[{ value: 'cards', label: 'Cards', show: '[data-grid]' }, { value: 'list', label: 'List', show: '[data-list]' }]}
            sort={{ options: [{ value: 'site', label: 'By office' }, { value: 'name', label: 'By name' }] }} />
        Order in the bar (rule book, words.md W5 and W6): find box, facets (Region, Office, Kind, Status, then the
        page's own), switches, Clear; then at the right anything inside the bar tag, the view switch, Sort,
        and always the count, "N of M rooms".
        views: word pills ("Cards | List"). Each view's `show` is a selector for the element it shows; the
          bar hides the others, holds the page still, recounts, remembers the choice in this browser
          (viewKey, default one per page) and fires "fb:view" with detail { value }. A view may carry its
          own `noun` ([one, many]) when the count should name something else there ("3 of 12 rooms" as
          cards, "5 of 61 units" as a list). A page sets the view from code with bar.rsFilter.setView(v).
        sort: a pill "Sort: By office" that opens like a facet, never a <select>. The bar keeps the choice in
          the address (?sort=name, left out for the first option) and fires "fb:sort" with detail { value };
          the page re-orders its items inside bar.rsFilter.run(true, reorder) so they slide into place.
          bar.rsFilter.set(key, values) sets a facet to exactly those choices (an empty list clears it; an object {role: [...], kind: [...]} sets several and recounts once);
          bar.rsFilter.sort() reads the choice; bar.rsFilter.setSort(value, label) shows a choice made
          elsewhere (a table heading) without firing.
     4. Add the empty state (EmptyState.astro, or any element with data-fb-none), hidden until nothing
        matches, with a <button data-fb-clear> inside it. Any element with data-fb-shown or data-fb-total
        gets those numbers.
     4b. A facet can be `single: true` (one choice at a time: choosing another drops the first) and can
        start on a choice: `value: 'cut'` (or an array for several). A facet with a starting choice is
        not "active" while it holds it, "Clear all" puts it back, and the address only names it when it
        differs (?situation=cut left out; ?status= for none). A single facet that starts on a choice is
        always on one: choosing the same again does nothing. Its list closes after a pick.
        The bar sets --fb-h (its height in px, 0 when it is not sticky) on <html>, for sticky headings
        that sit under it: top: calc(var(--mast-h) + var(--fb-h)). A facet list that would run off the
        right edge of the window opens towards the left by itself.
     5. A group of choices can also sit elsewhere on the page: an element with data-fb-facet="<key>" that holds
        buttons [data-fopt][data-v][data-label] (each may hold a [data-n] for its count).
   Hooks for the page: the bar (and document) gets "fb:change" with detail {shown, total, active}; a page that
   re-orders or swaps views calls bar.rsFilter.run(animate, beforeFn) or dispatches "rs:find-refresh" on document.
   Items whose data-f-* or data-find change after load (live updates): bar.rsFilter.refresh(el) re-reads that
   item (or every item inside el; no argument re-reads all), or dispatch "rs:find-refresh" with detail { el }. */
import Icon from './Icon.astro';

interface Option { value: string; label: string; sub?: string; swatch?: string }
interface Facet { key: string; label: string; options: Option[]; single?: boolean; value?: string | string[] }
interface Toggle { key: string; label: string; title?: string }
interface View { value: string; label: string; show?: string; noun?: [string, string] }
interface Sort { options: { value: string; label: string }[]; value?: string }
// `count` is kept so older pages still build; the count always shows now (words.md W6).
interface Props { facets?: Facet[]; toggles?: Toggle[]; placeholder?: string; label?: string; noun?: [string, string]; scope?: string; sticky?: boolean; count?: boolean; animate?: boolean; url?: boolean; views?: View[]; view?: string; viewKey?: string; viewsHelp?: string; sort?: Sort }
const { facets = [], toggles = [], placeholder = 'Find', label = 'Find', noun = ['item', 'items'], scope = '.content', sticky = true, animate = true, url = true, views = [], view, viewKey, sort, viewsHelp = 'filter.views' } = Astro.props;
const hasExtra = Astro.slots.has('default');
const sort0 = sort ? (sort.options.find((o) => o.value === sort.value) ?? sort.options[0]) : null;
const view0 = views.length ? (views.find((v) => v.value === view) ?? views[0]).value : '';
const chev = '<path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6" />';
// One id per bar, so the Filters button can name the group it opens.
const uid = `fb${Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 8)}`;
---
<div class:list={['fb', 'glass-bar', { 'fb-sticky': sticky }]} data-fb data-scope={scope} data-noun={noun[0]} data-nouns={noun[1]} data-animate={animate ? 'on' : 'off'} data-url={url ? 'on' : 'off'} data-view-key={views.length ? (viewKey ?? '') : undefined} data-view0={view0 || undefined} data-sort0={sort0?.value}>
  <label class="fb-search" data-help="filter.find"><Icon name="search" size={16} /><span class="sr-only">{label}</span><input type="search" placeholder={placeholder} autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" data-fb-q /></label>
  {(facets.length > 0 || toggles.length > 0) && (
    <button type="button" class="fb-filters" data-fb-sheet-open aria-expanded="false" aria-controls={`${uid}-facets`}><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6h16M7 12h10M10 18h4" /></svg>Filters<b class="fb-nact" data-fb-nact></b></button>
  )}
  <div class="fb-facets" id={`${uid}-facets`} data-fb-facets role="group" aria-label="Filters">
    <div class="fb-sheet-h"><b>Filters</b><button type="button" class="fb-clear fb-clear-sheet" data-fb-clear>Clear all</button><button type="button" class="btn small primary fb-done" data-fb-sheet-close>Show <span data-fb-shown></span></button></div>
    {facets.map((f) => (
      <div class="fb-chip" data-help={`filter.facet:${f.key}`} data-help-name={f.label} data-fb-facet={f.key} data-single={f.single ? '1' : undefined} data-default={f.value === undefined ? undefined : [].concat(f.value).join(',')}>
        <button type="button" class="fb-chip-btn" aria-haspopup="true" aria-expanded="false"><span>{f.label}</span><b class="fb-val" data-val></b><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="14" height="14" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6" /></svg></button>
        <div class={`fb-pop ${f.options.length > 8 ? 'wide' : ''}`} role="group" aria-label={f.label}>
          {f.options.map((o) => <button type="button" class="fb-opt" data-fopt data-v={o.value} data-label={o.label} aria-pressed="false"><span>{o.swatch && <i class="fb-sw" style={`--sw:${o.swatch}`}></i>}{o.label}{o.sub && <small>{o.sub}</small>}</span><i class="fb-n" data-n></i></button>)}
        </div>
      </div>
    ))}
    {toggles.map((t) => <button type="button" class="fb-toggle" data-help="filter.toggle" data-help-name={t.label} data-fb-toggle={t.key} aria-pressed="false" title={t.title}><span class="fb-tick" aria-hidden="true"></span>{t.label}</button>)}
    <button type="button" class="fb-clear fb-clear-bar" data-help="filter.clear" data-fb-clear hidden>Clear all</button>
  </div>
  <div class="fb-end">
    {hasExtra && <div class="fb-extra"><slot /></div>}
    {views.length > 1 && (
      <div class="fb-views" role="group" aria-label="View" data-help={viewsHelp}>
        {views.map((v) => <button type="button" class="fb-view" data-fb-view={v.value} data-show={v.show} data-noun={v.noun?.[0]} data-nouns={v.noun?.[1]} aria-pressed={v.value === view0 ? 'true' : 'false'}>{v.label}</button>)}
      </div>
    )}
    <div class="fb-sc">
    {sort0 && (
      <div class="fb-chip fb-sort" data-help="filter.sort" data-fb-sort>
        <button type="button" class="fb-chip-btn" aria-haspopup="true" aria-expanded="false"><span>Sort</span><b class="fb-val" data-sort-val>{sort0.label}</b><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="14" height="14" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true" set:html={chev}></svg></button>
        <div class="fb-pop end" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Sort">
          {sort!.options.map((o) => <button type="button" class="fb-opt" role="radio" data-sort-opt data-v={o.value} data-label={o.label} aria-checked={o.value === sort0.value ? 'true' : 'false'}><span>{o.label}</span></button>)}
        </div>
      </div>
    )}
    <span class="fb-count" data-help="filter.count" data-fb-count aria-live="polite"></span>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<script is:inline data-astro-rerun>
  (function () {
    var norm = function (s) { return String(s || '').normalize('NFD').replace(/[̀-ͯ]/g, '').toLowerCase(); };
    var fmt = function (n) { return n.toLocaleString('en-IE'); };
    // The items come after the bar in the page, so on a first load wait until the page is read.
    // Glass only while pinned: a 1px marker sits just above each sticky bar; once it has scrolled past the
    // line the bar pins to, the bar is stuck and gets its frosted background (.is-stuck in base.css).
    var watchStuck = function (bar) {
      if (!bar.classList.contains('fb-sticky') || bar.rsStuck) return;
      var mark = document.createElement('div'); mark.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true'); mark.style.cssText = 'height:1px;margin-bottom:-1px;pointer-events:none';
      bar.parentNode.insertBefore(mark, bar);
      var check = function () {
        if (!bar.isConnected) { window.removeEventListener('scroll', check); window.removeEventListener('resize', check); return; }
        var top = parseFloat(getComputedStyle(bar).top);
        bar.classList.toggle('is-stuck', getComputedStyle(bar).position === 'sticky' && mark.getBoundingClientRect().top < (isNaN(top) ? 60 : top));
      };
      bar.rsStuck = check;
      window.addEventListener('scroll', check, { passive: true }); window.addEventListener('resize', check, { passive: true }); check();
    };
    var start = function () { document.querySelectorAll('[data-fb]').forEach(function (b) { bind(b); watchStuck(b); }); };
    if (document.readyState === 'loading') document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', start, { once: true }); else start();

    function bind(bar) {
      if (bar.__fb) return;
      var scope = document.querySelector(bar.dataset.scope) || document.querySelector('.content') || document.body;
      var qi = bar.querySelector('[data-fb-q]'), countEl = bar.querySelector('[data-fb-count]'), clearBtns = bar.querySelectorAll('[data-fb-clear]'), nactEl = bar.querySelector('[data-fb-nact]');
      var one = bar.dataset.noun, many = bar.dataset.nouns, one0 = one, many0 = many, useUrl = bar.dataset.url !== 'off', canMove = bar.dataset.animate !== 'off';
      var facets = Array.prototype.slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('[data-fb-facet]'));
      var toggles = Array.prototype.slice.call(bar.querySelectorAll('[data-fb-toggle]'));
      var sel = {}, on = {}, q = '', cache = new WeakMap();
      // A facet may start on a choice (data-default) and may allow one choice only (data-single).
      var dflt = {};
      facets.forEach(function (f) { var k = f.dataset.fbFacet; sel[k] = new Set(); dflt[k] = (f.dataset.default || '').split(',').filter(Boolean); });
      toggles.forEach(function (t) { on[t.dataset.fbToggle] = false; });
      var qs = new URLSearchParams(location.search);
      // The address wins; a facet the address does not name starts on its default ("?k=" alone means none).
      Object.keys(sel).forEach(function (k) { (qs.has(k) ? qs.get(k) : dflt[k].join(',')).split(',').filter(Boolean).forEach(function (v) { sel[k].add(v); }); });
      Object.keys(on).forEach(function (k) { on[k] = qs.get(k) === '1'; });
      q = norm(qs.get('q') || '').trim(); qi.value = qs.get('q') || '';
      // Sort and view (words.md W6): a sort pill that opens like a facet, and word pills for the view.
      var sortChip = bar.querySelector('[data-fb-sort]'), sort0 = bar.dataset.sort0 || '', sortV = sort0;
      var sortOpts = sortChip ? Array.prototype.slice.call(sortChip.querySelectorAll('[data-sort-opt]')) : [];
      if (sortOpts.some(function (o) { return o.dataset.v === qs.get('sort'); })) sortV = qs.get('sort');
      var viewBtns = Array.prototype.slice.call(bar.querySelectorAll('[data-fb-view]'));
      var viewKey = 'rs4-view:' + (bar.dataset.viewKey || location.pathname), viewV = bar.dataset.view0 || '';
      if (viewBtns.length) { try { var sv = localStorage.getItem(bar.dataset.viewKey || viewKey); if (viewBtns.some(function (b) { return b.dataset.fbView === sv; })) viewV = sv; } catch (_) {} }

      // What one item says about itself: its text, its value for each facet, its switches. Read once.
      var info = function (el) {
        var c = cache.get(el); if (c) return c;
        c = { v: {}, t: {}, q: norm(el.getAttribute('data-find') || el.textContent) };
        for (var i = 0; i < el.attributes.length; i++) {
          var a = el.attributes[i];
          if (a.name.indexOf('data-f-') === 0) c.v[a.name.slice(7)] = a.value.split('|').filter(Boolean);
          else if (a.name.indexOf('data-t-') === 0) c.t[a.name.slice(7)] = a.value === '1';
        }
        cache.set(el, c); return c;
      };
      // What stops an item showing: the words, one facet, or one switch. Nothing listed means it shows.
      var misses = function (c, words) {
        var out = [], w, k, j, ok;
        for (w = 0; w < words.length; w++) if (c.q.indexOf(words[w]) < 0) { out.push('#q'); break; }
        for (k in sel) {
          if (!sel[k].size) continue;
          var v = c.v[k] || []; ok = false;
          for (j = 0; j < v.length; j++) if (sel[k].has(v[j])) { ok = true; break; }
          if (!ok) out.push(k);
        }
        for (k in on) if (on[k] && !c.t[k]) out.push('#t');
        return out;
      };
      var inHidden = function (el) { var p = el.closest('[hidden]'); return !!p && (scope === p || scope.contains(p)); };
      // A facet holding its starting choice is not a filter the viewer chose.
      var atDefault = function (k) { var s = sel[k]; return s.size === dflt[k].length && dflt[k].every(function (v) { return s.has(v); }); };
      var isActive = function () { return !!q || Object.keys(sel).some(function (k) { return !atDefault(k); }) || Object.keys(on).some(function (k) { return on[k]; }); };
      var visible = function (el) { return !el.classList.contains('fb-out') && !inHidden(el); };

      // Keep the address in step, so a filtered, sorted list can be shared.
      function syncUrl() {
        if (!useUrl) return;
        var p = new URLSearchParams();
        Object.keys(sel).forEach(function (k) { if (!atDefault(k)) p.set(k, Array.from(sel[k]).join(',')); });
        Object.keys(on).forEach(function (k) { if (on[k]) p.set(k, '1'); });
        if (qi.value.trim()) p.set('q', qi.value.trim());
        if (sortV && sortV !== sort0) p.set('sort', sortV);
        try { history.replaceState(history.state, '', location.pathname + (p.toString() ? '?' + p : '') + location.hash); } catch (_) {}
      }

      function run(animate, before) {
        var M = window.rsMotion ? window.rsMotion() : { reduced: (window.rsReducedNow ? window.rsReducedNow() : matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches), ease: 'cubic-bezier(.22,1,.36,1)', morph: 520, enter: 440, stagger: 24 };
        if (bar.__rsOut) { bar.__rsOut(); bar.__rsOut = null; }   // a quick second pick ends the last exits first
        var els = Array.prototype.slice.call(scope.querySelectorAll('[data-fi]'));
        var words = q ? q.split(/\s+/) : [];
        var counted = els.filter(function (el) { return !inHidden(el); });
        var move = animate && canMove && !M.reduced && counted.length <= 400;
        var was = new Map(), shows = new Map(), vh = innerHeight;
        var near = function (r) { return r.bottom > -60 && r.top < vh + 60; };
        if (move) counted.forEach(function (el) {
          if (el.classList.contains('fb-out')) return;
          var r = el.getBoundingClientRect(); was.set(el, r);
          if (near(r)) shows.set(el, getComputedStyle(el).display);
        });
        // The bar's own pills slide aside when one grows to name its choice (M12).
        var groups = move ? Array.prototype.slice.call(scope.querySelectorAll('[data-fb-group]:not(.fb-out)')).map(function (g) {
          var r = g.getBoundingClientRect(); return near(r) && !inHidden(g) ? [g, r, getComputedStyle(g).display] : null;
        }).filter(Boolean) : [];
        var parts = move ? Array.prototype.slice.call(bar.querySelectorAll('.fb-facets > .fb-chip, .fb-facets > .fb-toggle, .fb-facets > .fb-clear, .fb-end .fb-views, .fb-end .fb-chip, .fb-extra > *')) : [];
        var partsWas = parts.map(function (el) { return el.getBoundingClientRect(); });
        var apply = function () {
          if (before) before();
          els.forEach(function (el) { el.classList.toggle('fb-out', misses(info(el), words).length > 0); });
          Array.prototype.forEach.call(scope.querySelectorAll('[data-fb-group]'), function (g) { g.classList.toggle('fb-out', !g.querySelector('[data-fi]:not(.fb-out)')); });
        };
        if (window.rsHold && animate) {
          window.rsHold(scope, apply);
          if (window.scrollY < 4) scope.style.minHeight = '';
        } else apply();
        // Counts: what shows, and how many each choice would leave with everything else as it is.
        var shown = 0, total = counted.length, counts = {};
        Object.keys(sel).forEach(function (k) { counts[k] = {}; });
        counted.forEach(function (el) {
          var c = info(el), m = misses(c, words);
          if (!m.length) shown++;
          if (m.length > 1) return;
          Object.keys(sel).forEach(function (k) {
            if (m.length && m[0] !== k) return;
            var v = c.v[k] || []; for (var j = 0; j < v.length; j++) counts[k][v[j]] = (counts[k][v[j]] || 0) + 1;
          });
        });
        facets.forEach(function (f) {
          var k = f.dataset.fbFacet, s = sel[k], names = [];
          Array.prototype.forEach.call(f.querySelectorAll('[data-fopt]'), function (b) {
            var pressed = s.has(b.dataset.v), n = counts[k][b.dataset.v] || 0, ne = b.querySelector('[data-n]');
            b.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(pressed));
            if (ne) ne.textContent = n;
            b.classList.toggle('none', n === 0 && !pressed);
            if (pressed) names.push(b.dataset.label);
          });
          f.classList.toggle('on', s.size > 0);
          var val = f.querySelector('[data-val]');
          if (val) val.textContent = names.length > 1 ? names.length + ' chosen' : (names[0] || '');
        });
        toggles.forEach(function (t) { t.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(on[t.dataset.fbToggle])); });
        var active = isActive();
        scope.classList.toggle('fb-on', active);
        Array.prototype.forEach.call(clearBtns, function (b) { b.hidden = !active; });
        // Phones: the Filters button says how many choices are on.
        if (nactEl) {
          var nOn = Object.keys(sel).reduce(function (m, k) { return m + (atDefault(k) ? 0 : sel[k].size); }, 0) + Object.keys(on).filter(function (k) { return on[k]; }).length;
          nactEl.textContent = nOn ? String(nOn) : '';
        }
        // Always "N of M", so the count keeps its width and place as filters come and go; a new number ticks in.
        if (countEl) {
          countEl.textContent = fmt(shown) + ' of ' + fmt(total) + ' ' + (total === 1 ? one : many);
          // The new number ticks into place (km-tick; the library's figure watcher in src/lib/motion-wire.js sees the change).
          // The page added items since the bar was laid out (a list drawn by its script): make room once.
          if (bar.rsLayout && countEl.scrollWidth > (parseFloat(countEl.style.minWidth) || 0) + 1) bar.rsLayout();
        }
        Array.prototype.forEach.call(document.querySelectorAll('[data-fb-shown]'), function (e) { e.textContent = fmt(shown); });
        Array.prototype.forEach.call(document.querySelectorAll('[data-fb-total]'), function (e) { e.textContent = fmt(total); });
        Array.prototype.forEach.call(document.querySelectorAll('[data-fb-none]'), function (e) { e.hidden = shown > 0 || total === 0; });
        syncUrl();
        var detail = { shown: shown, total: total, active: active };
        bar.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('fb:change', { bubbles: true, detail: detail }));
        // Motion (M2, M12): things that stay slide to their new place, things that arrive grow from their
        // centre, things that leave shrink to theirs where they were (rsEnterEls and rsExitEls in the Shell).
        if (move) {
          var ins = [], outs = groups.filter(function (g) { return g[0].classList.contains('fb-out'); });
          counted.forEach(function (el) {
            var a = was.get(el);
            if (el.classList.contains('fb-out')) { if (a && shows.has(el) && !el.closest('[data-fb-group].fb-out')) outs.push([el, a, shows.get(el)]); return; }
            var b = el.getBoundingClientRect();
            if (!near(b) && !(a && near(a))) return;
            if (a) {
              var dx = a.left - b.left, dy = a.top - b.top;
              if (Math.abs(dx) + Math.abs(dy) > 0.5) el.animate([{ transform: 'translate(' + dx + 'px,' + dy + 'px)' }, { transform: 'none' }], { duration: M.morph, easing: M.ease });
            } else ins.push([el, b]);
          });
          if (window.rsExitEls) bar.__rsOut = window.rsExitEls(outs);
          if (window.rsEnterEls) window.rsEnterEls(ins);
          parts.forEach(function (el, i) {
            var a = partsWas[i], b = el.getBoundingClientRect(), dx = a.left - b.left, dy = a.top - b.top;
            if (b.width && a.width && Math.abs(dx) + Math.abs(dy) > 0.5) el.animate([{ transform: 'translate(' + dx + 'px,' + dy + 'px)' }, { transform: 'none' }], { duration: M.morph, easing: M.ease });
          });
        }
        return detail;
      }

      var clearAll = function () {
        Object.keys(sel).forEach(function (k) { sel[k].clear(); dflt[k].forEach(function (v) { sel[k].add(v); }); });
        Object.keys(on).forEach(function (k) { on[k] = false; });
        q = ''; qi.value = ''; run(true);
      };
      var pick = function (k, v, single) {
        var s = sel[k];
        if (single) { if (s.has(v)) { if (dflt[k].length) return; s.delete(v); } else { s.clear(); s.add(v); } }
        else if (s.has(v)) s.delete(v); else s.add(v);
        run(true);
      };

      // A pill that opens its list: hover opens it; a click keeps it open until a second click, Escape,
      // or a click elsewhere; keyboard focus opens it too. Facets and Sort both work this way.
      // A list that would run past the right edge of the window opens towards the left instead.
